.TH GROTTO-DAEMON 1 "October 2026" "Grotto Preview 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grotto-daemon \- post-login Nostr signing service (Preview)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grotto-daemon
[\fB\-\-bunker\fR] [\fB\-\-no-approval-ui\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
One daemon per user session owns org.nostr.Signer. Local NIP-55L, optional
NIP-5F socket and remote NIP-46 requests use the same scoped permission gate.
D-Bus activates the daemon on demand. Do not run a second copy beside the unit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-bunker
Start configured remote signing; explicit relays and transport custody required.
.TP
.B \-\-no-approval-ui
Suppress approver activation. Pre-approved scoped work can continue; new consent
fails closed with a typed NoApprovalAgent error. This is not allow-all mode.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show supported options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the component build version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOSTR_SIGNER_ENDPOINT
Opt into a NIP-5F socket, e.g. unix:$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/gnostr/signer.sock.
No socket is exposed by default. TCP is not the supported release path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gnostr/signer-permissions-v2.ini
Scoped permissions; broad legacy event allows migrate to non-executable review.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/grotto/
Daemon-owned clients, bunker configuration, replay fences and metadata activity.
Keep directories 0700 and files 0600; preserve replay state across restart.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/grotto/examples/
Explicit bunker and headless network drop-in examples. Install exactly one as a
user override, reload systemd and restart once. Live ConfigureBunker needs no restart.
.SH SECURITY
Client methods do not return private keys. Explicit trusted Grotto key management
can handle them. Signing is not publication. Same-user malware is outside the
boundary; PID-attested Linux retains installed executable path/inode checks.
UID-only buses have weaker inherited caller isolation.
.PP
The shipped namespace-free user unit preserves host /proc access and allows only
localhost network traffic. Remote relays require the explicit network drop-in.
There is no SIGHUP reload. Do not add mount-namespace hardening that breaks callers.
Use Pause signing, not window lock or Quit, to stop remembered signing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grotto (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
